  "notes": "City Cement Company (ticker 3003, a Saudi Joint Stock Company) audited consolidated financial statements for the year ended 31 December 2025 with FY2024 comparatives, from the full audited PDF in the 'Annual / 2025' cell of the Saudi Exchange company-profile 'Financial Statements' tab (Resources/fsPdf/421_0_2026-03-24...). Auditor: BDO Dr. Mohamed Al-Amri & Co.; unqualified opinion. The consolidated financial statements were approved by the Board of Directors on 27 Ramadan 1447H (corresponding to 16 March 2026) - Note 35. Amounts are presented in full Saudi Riyals (scale 1) except per-share data. The auditor's report and the primary statements (printed FS pages 5-8) are scanned images in the filed PDF (transcribed from page renders at 2.6x; the scans have their label and value columns slightly offset - figures were aligned by note number and by checking each subtotal); the notes are digital text. Consolidated group (with an equity-accounted joint venture); there is **NO non-controlling interest** (net profit and equity are not split), so only total_equity is carried. There are no discontinued operations - the standard pre-tax - zakat bridge applies. **The Group has no bank debt** - the only borrowings are IFRS 16 lease liabilities (lease_liabilities_noncurrent / lease_liabilities_current). investments_joint_ventures is 'Investments in Joint Venture'; share_of_profit_associates is 'Group's share in losses from joint venture' (a loss both years); long_term_investments is 'Investments in equity instruments at fair value through other comprehensive income'; short_term_investments combines the current 'Investments in Financial instruments at fair value through profit or loss' (SAR 394,563,647) and the 'Short term time deposit' (SAR 146,000,000); accounts_receivable is 'Trade receivables'; related_party_receivables is 'Due From Related Party' (nil FY2024); prepayments is 'Prepayments and other receivables'; cash is the balance-sheet 'Cash and cash equivalents' line. other_reserves is the 'Reserve for revaluation of financial investments at fair value through OCI'; defined_benefit_obligation is 'Employees' end-of-service benefits'; provisions is 'Provision for rehabilitation of areas subject to franchise license' (quarry / franchise); accrued_expenses is 'Accrual and other payables'; zakat_payable is 'Provision for zakat'. On the P&L: operating_income is 'Operating profit'; other_nonoperating_income is 'Gains of changes in fair value of investments in financial instruments through profit or loss'; other_nonoperating_expense is '(Losses) from sale of Property, plant and equipment' (nil FY2024); other_income is 'Other income'; impairment_charges is 'provision for expected credit losses'; finance_costs is 'Finance cost'; income_taxes_and_zakat is 'Zakat expense'. On the cash-flow statement: depreciation_amortization is the single 'Depreciation and Amortisation' add-back; zakat_paid is 'Zakat paid'; capex is 'Purchase of property, plant and equipment and Capital work in progress' (plus 'Purchase of intangible assets' in FY2024); dividends_paid is 'Dividends paid'; lease_payments is 'Repayments of lease liability'; the cash-flow statement discloses no separate finance-cost-paid line, so interest_paid is not carried, and it has no FX-on-cash line. **The cash-flow 'Cash and cash equivalents at the end of the year' (SAR 113,777,135) is SAR 100,000,000 higher than the balance-sheet 'Cash and cash equivalents' line (SAR 13,777,135)** because the cash-flow definition includes short-term time deposits with an original maturity of three months or less; the two agree at 31 December 2024 (SAR 42,358,215). This makes the cash-flow-to-balance-sheet cross-check warn for FY2025 only (expected). **Softer year** - cost of revenues rose while revenue was flat, taking gross margin from 36.2% to 31.5%, operating profit to SAR 113.2m and net profit to SAR 128.9m (EPS 0.92, FY2024 1.03). Statement page references are the printed FS page numbers: financial position 5, profit or loss and OCI 6, changes in equity 7, cash flows 8.",
